	(descr "onsemi/Fairchild FDMC2523P, single P-Channel QFET MOSFET (-150V/-3A, RDS(on)=1.5ohm typ), package = 'Power33-8' (onsemi's own naming, LCSC listing C890927), a.k.a. WDFN-8, body 3.3x3.3x0.75mm, 0.65mm pitch, 4+4 dual-row leadframe. Datasheet source: onsemi FDMC2523P-D (onsemi.com/pdf/datasheet/fdmc2523p-d.pdf), marking diagram gives lead sequence 'S G S S | D D D D' (pin1=S,2=G,3=S,4=S on one side; pin5-8=D on the other), i.e. 3 paralleled source pads + 1 gate pad + 4 paralleled drain pads for low RDS(on). Pad size/pitch/column-offset geometry adapted from the real stock KiCad footprint 'Package_SON.pretty/Fairchild_DualPower33-6_3x3mm.kicad_mod' (same Fairchild 'Power 33' 3x3mm leadframe family, same 0.65mm pitch, verified column x-offset -1.39/+1.39mm), scaled from 6 to 8 discrete pads since no stock 8-pin variant of this package exists. Pad numbers use S/G/D strings (not 1-8) to match this project's Device:Q_PMOS symbol pin numbering for Q21. Placeholder guess 'QFN-8_2x2mm' was wrong on both body size (2x2mm vs real 3.3x3.3mm) and implied single-pad-per-pin layout. APPROXIMATION FLAG: top/bottom physical ordering of the 4 pins per side (exact match to datasheet's physical marking orientation, vs. mirrored) is inferred from standard counterclockwise QFN/MLP numbering, not confirmed against a literal onsemi mechanical land-pattern drawing (unavailable in machine-readable form); pad-name (S/G/D) electrical correctness does not depend on this ordering.")
	(tags "FDMC2523P PMOS Power33-8 WDFN QFET")
